8:T6cc,{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What makes the Gravity Cart Sport different from other gravity carts?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"It is a single convertible chassis with certified wheel and ski assemblies included, so it covers pavement, gravel and packed snow. Its figures are published: rated load 120 kg, ski assembly rated to 25% descent grade on packed snow, brakes tested to ECE R100, fork in 304 stainless steel."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is there an all-season gravity cart?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The Gravity Cart Sport (GC-SPORT-01, €2,890.00) is built for year-round use. The same chassis runs on wheels for pavement and gravel and on the Ski Assembly Kit for packed snow. Both assemblies are included."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much weight can the Gravity Cart Sport carry?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The rated load is 120 kg."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What descent grade is the ski conversion rated for?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The Ski Assembly Kit (GC-SKI-200) is rated to a 25% descent grade on packed snow. It has a 780 mm ski length and a tool-free binding."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Which brakes does the Gravity Cart Sport use and are they tested?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The Shimano Dual Brake Kit (GC-BRK-180) is a hydraulic dual-disc set with 180 mm front and rear rotors, tested to ECE R100."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Where can I buy it and what does it cost?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Directly from GravityCart through this site, with no third-party dealer network. The Gravity Cart Sport costs €2,890.00."}}]}0:{"P":null,"b":"yNmA_oew2rdrZXTCE1_6K","p":"","c":["","why-gravitycart"],"i":false,"f":[[["",{"children":["why-gravitycart",{"children":["__PAGE__",{}]}]},"$undefined","$undefined",true],["",["$","$1","c",{"children":[[["$","link","0",{"rel":"stylesheet","